[{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/netty/netty/issues/comments/327182455","html_url":"https://github.com/netty/netty/issues/7179#issuecomment-327182455","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/netty/netty/issues/7179","id":327182455,"node_id":"MDEyOklzc3VlQ29tbWVudDMyNzE4MjQ1NQ==","user":{"login":"Apache9","id":4958168,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ5NTgxNjg=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/4958168?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Apache9","html_url":"https://github.com/Apache9","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Apache9/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Apache9/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Apache9/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Apache9/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Apache9/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Apache9/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Apache9/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Apache9/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Apache9/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2017-09-05T13:54:45Z","updated_at":"2017-09-05T13:54:45Z","body":"The problem is that the `writable` field for server side `DefaultHttp2StreamChannel` is always `false`. \r\n\r\nAt client side, the `writable` will be changed after calling the `onStreamActive` in the `Http2ConnectionAdapter` of `DefaultHttp2RemoteFlowController`. It will finally reach the `DefaultHttp2StreamChannel.writabilityChanged`.\r\n\r\nBut at server side, the calling trace is broken up at `Http2FrameCodec.Http2RemoteFlowControllerListener.writabilityChanged`. In this method, the `Http2FrameStream` gotten from the `Http2Stream` is null, so we give up.\r\n\r\nhttps://github.com/netty/netty/blob/4.1/codec-http2/src/main/java/io/netty/handler/codec/http2/Http2FrameCodec.java#L588\r\n\r\nNo ide